EXT. CHURCH BELFRY, HOLLOWED VILLAGE - DAY

A shattered belfry overlooking a flooded field. A stagnant afternoon. Rain has stopped but the sky has not made up its mind.

SERGEANT NIKOLAI VASSILIEV (30s, tired, frost in his beard) sits on an ammunition crate, cleaning a rifle bolt with a rag, while PRIVATE ANNELIESE BRANDSTETTER (20s, a nurse's armband stitched crooked over her sleeve) rewraps a bandage and a fresh-faced boy, PRIVATE YUSUF DEMIR (19), watches the field through a gap in the stones and a radioman, CORPORAL HARLAN PIKE (40s, headset askew), lights a cigarette, drags on it, hands it to Yusuf, and takes the binoculars back without looking.

A scrap of white cloth drifts across the flooded field, snagged on a pole that bobs and turns in the current. Beneath it, something pale struggles in the water.

SERGEANT
Hold your fire. Let it come.

YUSUF
It's a dog, Sergeant.

NIKOLAI
It's a dog with a cloth round its neck. Wait.

ANNELIESE
It's limping.

PIKE
Could be a trick.

ANNELIESE
Could be a leg.

The dog stumbles in the water. Anneliese rises, but Nikolai catches her sleeve.

NIKOLAI
Wait.

She waits. Pike mutters into the handset, lowers it, and shrugs. Yusuf passes the cigarette back. Nikolai sets his rifle bolt on the crate, wipes his hands, and nods once.

NIKOLAI (CONT'D)
Go and get it.

Anneliese and Yusuf start down the stone steps together. Pike watches them go. Nikolai goes back to the bolt.

PIKE
You'd have let it drown.

SERGEANT
I'd have let it choose.

He slides the bolt home. It clicks.
